{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790351688,"nonce":"KJgRnpORyW4c+krl9/N0BcAE1rU=","message":"c3da909: nbody's module body (its only loop calls sim.advance and counts) is no longer compiled by LLVM ahead of advance on the single LLVM thread. advance's LLVM body now installs at ~62 ms instead of ~80 ms (NUC, i5-1250P).\n\nNUC A/B, median of 7, ce0345e -\u003e c3da909:\n  cores 0-15: nbody 0.0968 -\u003e 0.0823; delta_blue 0.0783 -\u003e 0.0742; others within noise\n  cores 0-3:  nbody 0.0919 -\u003e 0.0809; others within noise\n  cores 0-1:  nbody 0.1229 -\u003e 0.0995; others within noise\nLuaJIT nbody on the same runs: 0.068-0.079.\n\nWhere the 500k-step run goes (nbody at N steps, c3da909):\n  N=10k 17.9 ms, 50k 30.2, 100k 43.6, 200k 63.8, 300k 70.8, 500k 83.6, 1M 114.7\n  -\u003e first 10k steps (interpreter + baseline) ~1.8 us/step; Cranelift optimised ~200-270 ns/step; LLVM ~62 ns/step\n  LuaJIT: 10k 2.4 ms, 100k 14.3, 500k 64.5, 1M 130.5 -\u003e ~130 ns/step\n  So LLVM code is 2x LuaJIT at steady state; the gap is warm-up.\n\nRejected experiments (NUC, nbody 500k unless noted):\n  direct to LLVM (skip Cranelift optimised): nbody 0.078 but method_call 2x slower, mandelbrot +13%, dyn_dispatch +17%\n  two LLVM threads: nbody -10% but method_call +15%, mandelbrot +13%, delta_blue +25% on 4 cores\n  MCJIT codegen level 1: no compile-time saving; level 0: 5M steps 0.515 vs 0.372\n\nHyperthread contention: the i5-1250P's P-cores are hyperthreaded. A busy sibling slows the main thread 0.042 -\u003e 0.070 (Cranelift-only, 100k steps); a busy E-core barely (0.044). The LLVM compile of advance (~40 ms) therefore also slows the Cranelift optimised code running beside it: at 100k steps Cranelift-only 0.0335 vs default 0.0436. A 4-vCPU CI runner (2 cores x 2 threads) sees the same.\n\nLLVM pipeline (advance compile: build+opt cumulative ms / codegen ms):\n  O2 + unswitch (current): opt 19.3, codegen 14.0; nbody 0.0846, 5M 0.367, ash/nbody 0.677\n  P6 = sroa,early-cse\u003cmemssa\u003e,instcombine,simplifycfg,loop-mssa(loop-rotate,licm\u003callowspeculation\u003e,simple-loop-unswitch\u003cnontrivial\u003e),gvn,slp-vectorizer,instcombine,simplifycfg\n       opt ~11, nbody 0.0756, ash/nbody 0.698 (+3.5%)\n  P8 = P6 with jump-threading,correlated-propagation after gvn\n       nbody 0.0749, ash/nbody 0.656, ash/mandelbrot 0.242\n  Broad A/B of P8 pending a quiet box.","files":null}]}